+    runs from our last successful FETCH. It says nothing about how old the
+    MEASUREMENT inside that payload is, and the two come apart in the case this
+    fixture builds: the upstream answers promptly with a station whose
+    ``last_update`` stopped moving hours ago, so the payload is fresh by our
+    clock and ancient by the station's. ``waqi.MAX_OBS_AGE`` is the bound on the
+    measurement, and the ``_TTL_RETAIN`` comment cites it as the outer bound
+    precisely because a held payload keeps its own obs_time.
